//  The {name} in the URL is the year's name, e.g. 2026-2027.
// ===========================================================================
//
//  NAME IS NOT ACCEPTED HERE — not optional, ABSENT from the request. A year's
//  name is the string every other collection stores to point at it.
//
//  Send either date or both. An omitted date is left alone.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 01  EXTEND THE END DATE                                 -> 200 OK
//     The body above. Extending is usually harmless.
//     OUT: durationDays grows; holidayCount unchanged.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// 02  MOVE THE START FORWARD                              -> 200 OK
// {
//   "startDate": "2026-06-01"
// }
//     Allowed while every existing holiday still falls inside the new range.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// 03  MOVE BOTH AT ONCE                                   -> 200 OK
